          "text": "Clinical Indication:  \nEvaluation of generalized epilepsy with generalized tonic-clonic seizures, with reported onset at age 62 and a frequency of approximately 2 seizures per week. Etiology is genetic, associated with an SCN1A c.5734C>T variant. The epilepsy is reported as drug-responsive. Current antiseizure medications are carbamazepine and brivaracetam.\n\nTechnique:  \nRoutine scalp EEG with standard clinical neurophysiology recording montage and simultaneous video monitoring.\n\nFindings:  \nThe authorized clinical information does not provide the EEG background, interictal epileptiform activity, or ictal electrographic findings. No additional EEG findings are reported.\n\nImpression:  \nEEG interpretation is limited because specific EEG findings were not provided. Clinical history is notable for generalized epilepsy with generalized tonic-clonic seizures, genetic etiology related to an SCN1A c.5734C>T variant, reported onset at age 62, frequency of 2 seizures per week, and current treatment with carbamazepine and brivaracetam.",
